        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "[V2G20-2083] The SECCID shall match the following structure (the notation corresponds to the augmented Backus-Naur Form (ABNF) as defined in IETF RFC 5234 and IETF RFC 7405):",
            "block_bbox": [
                69,
                340,
                1051,
                415
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 4,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    69.0,
                    340.0
                ],
                [
                    1051.0,
                    340.0
                ],
                [
                    1051.0,
                    415.0
                ],
                [
                    69.0,
                    415.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "algorithm",
            "block_content": "<SECCID> = <Country Code> <S> <EVSE Operator ID> <S> <ID Type>\n<S> <ControllerID> <S> <Check Digit>\n\n<Country Code> = 2 ALPHA\n\n; two character country code according to ISO 3166-1 (Alpha-2-Code)\n\n<EVSE Operator ID> = 3 (ALPHA / DIGIT)\n\n; three alphanumeric characters, referring to the EVSE Operator\n\n<ID Type> = \"S\"\n\n; one character \"S\" indicating that this ID represents a reference to a \"Supply Equipment\"\n\n<ControllerID> = Minimum 32 (ALPHA / DIGIT)\nMaximum 248 (ALPHA / DIGIT)\n\n; Alphanumeric characters referring to the specific communication controller\n\n<Check Digit> = *1 (ALPHA / DIGIT)\n\n; Used to verify valid SECCID, see sub-clause C.6 for its computation\n\nALPHA = %x41-5A / %x61-7A\n\n; according to IETF RFC 5234 (7-Bit ASCII), case-insensitive (IETF RFC 7405)\n\nDIGIT = %x30-39\n\n; according to IETF RFC 5234 (7-Bit ASCII)\n\n<S> = *1 (\"-\" )\n\n; optional separator, but advised not to use it between IT systems and only for visibility purposes",
            "block_bbox": [
                280,
                429,
                1057,
                1455
            ],
